cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use research-kit, please cite it as below. A paper describing the
  method is in preparation and will supersede this repository-level entry
  when it is posted.
title: >-
  research-kit: agent skills for running a research project as checked records,
  with a reference library, a dashboard, working rules, and a checked prover
  handoff and landing for Lean
abstract: >-
  research-kit is two plugins for coding agents (Claude Code, Codex and any
  agent that reads the Agent Skills layout). The research plugin keeps a
  project's ideas, questions with kill criteria, tasks and findings as typed
  Markdown records moved through their states by transitions, and one card per
  cited work recording how far it was read and what may be claimed from it; a
  check on every commit fails a hand-edited state, a citation of a work with no
  card or one nobody read, and evidence that does not resolve. It adds a
  read-only dashboard over both and working rules for review, evidence, design
  and debugging. The formal plugin serves a project with a Lean 4 library: the
  prompt a prover session gets is checked before it is sent, and the session's
  report is verified against the built tree, by the declaration manifest's diff
  and a cold read-back of each landed statement, before any document changes.
  Every tool is a single Python 3.11 script on the standard library, and all
  data is plain Markdown in the project's repository.
type: software
